{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Come, etc.</b> And with the money they take by violence they will indulge themselves to drink, and the shepherd says to his fellow: Come, let us take wine." "<b>And let us drink our fill.</b> From שכר, like אַל־תְּהִי בְסֹבְאֵי־יָיִן (Proverbs 23:20). And they will not do for one day alone, but day after day." "<b>Abundantly.</b> An epithet of the name, that tomorrow's day will have excess over today's day in pleasure and in banqueting."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:52.052368581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}